	(text "OUTPUT TRANSIENT CLAMP\nD15: positive short pulses; D16: negative flyback.\nNo sustained external source allowed at LOAD_OUT.\nPulse energy and repetitive heating require bench validation."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 330.2 419.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9de8bb86-3204-47e4-bc16-8e6d2e2779f9")
	)
	(text "POWER MONITOR (PG) -- see docs/hardware-specification.md\nU10A VIN_UV, U10B 5V_UV, U10D OVP mirror: open-collector wired-AND -> POWER_GOOD.\nPOWER_GOOD LOW -> Q9 opens Q5 emitter -> load switch OFF, independent of firmware.\nPG pull-up from V_IN_REV_PROTECTED: a dead comparator cannot grant permission above Vin.\nR63 47k pulls PG to ~Vin/2: PB14 sees LOW for any Vin < ~2.3 V even with U10 unpowered.\nR60/C17: Q9 may conduct again ~0.14-0.31 ms after PG returns; D18 fast turn-off. PB14 EXTI must drop MCU_ENABLE.\nHW_OCP latch U7 shares V_BLUEPILL_3V3 with the MCU. POR flag does NOT prove the latch lost state;\nfirmware keeps an HW_OCP record in Flash (PB12 EXTI) to tell real faults from random power-up state."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40.64 530.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d029c927-6839-4a68-aa95-6bc82ef00d5c")
	)
	(text "Q7: UMW AO3400A (G1 S2 D3).\nHardware shutdown still overrides MCU_ENABLE.\nR29/R30 reduce DC loading of the HC00 latch."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 345.44 292.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f91d1d6e-f587-428c-b2b1-b041e312e75c")
	)
